                <h2>17. U.S. State Privacy Rights</h2>
                <p>This section is for users covered by U.S. state privacy laws such as the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA).</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Sale and sharing</strong>: we do not sell personal information for money. However, the device identifiers and ad interactions shared with Google for ads during free use (Section 2) may count as "sharing" personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising, or as "targeted advertising", under some state laws.</li>
                    <li><strong>How to opt out</strong>: decline tracking on iOS, delete your advertising ID on Android, make a choice in Settings › Ad privacy choices if it appears in the App, or buy Pro (Section 6). You can also email <a href="#" data-email-user="privacy" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">privacy (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Your rights</strong>: you may ask to know (access), correct or delete the personal information we hold and use the opt-out above, and we will not discriminate against you for doing so. Send requests to the email above; if we deny a request, we will explain why, and you may appeal by replying to the same address. The only information we hold is usage statistics and email inquiries; your habit names and what you logged never leave your device.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>18. GDPR (European Economic Area, UK, Switzerland)</h2>
                <p>If you are located in the EEA, the UK or Switzerland, you have additional rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (and the UK GDPR or the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection), including the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict processing, data portability, and object to processing, and the right to withdraw your consent at any time in Settings › Ad privacy choices (withdrawing consent to store and/or access information on a device also stops usage statistics). You may also lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority. Contact us at <a href="#" data-email-user="privacy" data-email-domain="pifl-labs.com"><span class="email-text">privacy (at) pifl-labs.com</span></a>.</p>

                <h2>19. Changes to this Policy</h2>
                <p>This Privacy Policy is effective as of October 27, 2026. Any changes will be announced on this page.</p>
